---
name: Org KPI evidence per-file targeting
description: Per-file employee/department targeting on Org KPI supporting files. Empty arrays = applies to everyone in scope (backward compatible). Resync filters per-employee.
type: feature
---
Each entry in `org_kpi_values.evidence_files` (JSONB) carries optional
`applies_to_employee_ids` and `applies_to_department_ids` arrays.

Rules (enforced in `_filter_files_for_employee` and `resync_org_kpi_evidence`):
- Both arrays empty/null → file applies to every mapped employee (legacy default; the common org-wide certificate case).
- Otherwise → file applies if `employee_id` is in `applies_to_employee_ids` OR the employee's `department_id` is in `applies_to_department_ids`.
- Per-employee scope OKVs ignore targeting (always 1:1).

Resync paths:
- `append_only` adds only the filtered URLs missing from each employee's `review_submissions.self_evidence_urls`.
- `replace_with_stepback` replaces with the filtered list; rows past `self_review` are sent back to `self_review` and audited as `ORG_KPI_EVIDENCE_STEPBACK`.

Visibility:
- `org_kpi_evidence_targeting(p_okv_id)` returns per-employee `{expected_files, current_urls, drift_kind}` driving the Distribution Preview in `OrgKpiEvidenceManagerSheet`.
- Targeting changes are audited via `ORG_KPI_EVIDENCE_TARGETING_CHANGED` (trigger `trg_audit_okv_evidence_targeting`).

UI:
- `EvidenceTargetPopover` (per file row) — employees/departments tabs, search, "Reaches N of M" live counter.
- `DistributionPreview` (panel under file list) — read-only matrix answering "which supporting goes to which employee".
